Everything else is ready — I just verified in WSL2:

| | |
|---|---|
| torch 2.14.1+cu130, CUDA | ✅ |
| GPU, bf16, 7.4 of 8.6 GB free | ✅ |
| unsloth / trl / peft / bitsandbytes | ✅ |
| `train.jsonl` — 60 examples | ✅ |
| **C compiler (gcc/cc)** | ❌ **missing** |

Triton JIT-compiles CUDA kernels at the first training step, and there's no `gcc`, `cc`, or `make` in your WSL install. `setup_wsl_training.sh` only ever installs `curl` and `ca-certificates`, so it reported `RESULT: READY` while leaving this hole — its CUDA matmul test passes on prebuilt kernels and never exercises Triton's JIT path.

**The blocker for me specifically:** `sudo` in your WSL needs a password, so I can't install it. That's your one command:

```
! wsl -d Ubuntu -- sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y build-essential
```

